# Frontend Rules

- Frontend lives in `Frontend/TripNova-angular-app/` — Angular 22 (standalone components, signals, SSR/prerender), Tailwind v4, Vitest.
- Requires Node ≥ 22.22.3 (Angular CLI check). Run with `npm start` (dev server on 4200).
- Backend API runs at `smart-travel-backend/` (FastAPI on default port 8000). Routes are **not** `/api/`-prefixed.
- API base URL comes from `src/environments/environment*.ts` (`apiBaseUrl`) — never hardcode it.
- Structure:
  - `src/app/core/models/` — API request/response types mirroring `smart-travel-backend/app/models.py`
  - `src/app/core/services/` — `HttpClient` wrappers (one service per backend area, e.g. `TravelApiService`)
  - `src/app/layout/` — app chrome (`dashboard-shell`: sidebar + top bar + `<router-outlet>`)
  - `src/app/features/<feature>/` — routed pages (`*-page.ts/html`) and feature components
- File naming follows Angular 20+ style: `plan-trip-page.ts` exporting `PlanTripPage` (no `.component` suffix).
- Design tokens (colours, type scale, fonts) are defined once in `src/styles.css` under `@theme`; use those utilities
  (`bg-surface-container`, `text-headline-xl`, `font-headline`) rather than raw hex values.
- Every network call must have loading, error and (where applicable) empty states.
- Co-locate specs (`*.spec.ts`); use `provideHttpClientTesting()` for service/page tests — never hit the real backend in tests.
